{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 and Mathlib proof that the Gallai–van der Waerden numbers GW(r; 3, 4) of Mao, Ozeki, Robertson and Wang equal 53 for r = 3, 4 and 5. GW(r; 3, l) is the least m such that for every n ≥ m, every exact r-colouring of {1, …, n} contains a rainbow 3-term or a monochromatic l-term arithmetic progression. Upper bound: for every r ≤ 5 and every n ≥ 53, every r-colouring of {1, …, n} has a rainbow 3-term or a monochromatic 4-term progression. This is reduced to the unsatisfiability of a CNF with 265 atoms and 43,562 clauses (colours renamed in order of first appearance), and the unsatisfiability is checked in Lean's kernel (decide +kernel, no native_decide) from an LRAT certificate of 1,211 derived clauses by a bitmask unit-propagation checker whose soundness is proved in Lean for every input. Lower bound: explicit exact 3-, 4- and 5-colourings of {1, …, 52} with neither progression, checked by the kernel. Together: GW(3; 3, 4) = GW(4; 3, 4) = GW(5; 3, 4) = 53.",
  "authors": [
